{
"v":1,
"show":"Kaskade feat. deadmau5 - I Remember",
"about":"Bars of a measured grid, shows/scenes/Kaskade feat. deadmau5 - I Remember.beats: bar b starts at 1.590 + 1.875 b seconds, 128.000 BPM, flat to 5 ms across the song, 151 bars. The bar line is where the chords turn: the song is one cycle, B A G G F# A G G, every change on a bar, starting on bar 2, 2 + 8n until the six bars on G before bar 102, 102 + 8n after them. The kick lands on bar 18 and again on bar 102, stops on 66 and 142. MEMORY, the most tender show of the set. A photograph develops from dark in sepia, burnt at its edge, with dust in the light and, slowly, two small figures holding hands, drawn on the dome where LEDs exist. Colour bleeds in: dusk, rose at the jaw, lavender on the brow, sea glass at the crown. On the first kick there is first light, a warm bloom on the shell and a slow ring going out through head and ears. Every four bars, on the turn of the chords, another ring goes out and dims. The ears breathe and never strobe: they inhale into each turn and exhale after it, and their colour is the chord, rose for B, lavender for A, sea glass for G, amber for F#, so the ears play the progression while the shell keeps time only with a soft pump and the rims with the kick. From bar 35 each sung line is a single pale light rising round the edge of the shell, its afterimage behind it in the complementary colour, and as it dissolves it goes up into the ear on its side. The long note on bar 48 hangs at the crown, and the hook is the picture in full colour, drifting like cloud. When the kick stops on 66 the colour drains back to sepia and the memory breaks up: three flickers, one side, the other side, then both with the two figures, each one followed by a bar of almost nothing, and in the last silent bar only their afterimage is left, in teal. The bass comes back on 82 at blue hour, stars and the ears breathing in turn. The title crosses once, slowly, on the voice's long note from 96 to 102, set high enough on the dome for its letters to land on LEDs, while the ears take six bars to breathe in. Bar 102 is the sunrise rather than an impact: a warm bloom on the returning kick, then over eight bars a half sun rises to the dome's horizon, its rays fanning across the brow. It stays through the second half and the colours of the hook come back into its rays. On 134 the music thins and the photograph yellows, with the two figures back in it. On 142 the kick stops for good, one last pale light rises, the tubes go out one at a time, the figures fade and a faint heart develops in their place, the only time it appears, and it outlasts the music by two bars. Text is the title only. Nothing on the shell pulses faster than a beat. For the long set the song averages 11.5 W: the shell is dark around its one bright thing (the sun at the jaw, a line's light, the disc on the horizon), the ears breathe as a band of light rather than a fill, and the rims only tick the kick. No limit was raised.",
